1
00:00:00,727 --> 00:00:03,197
"If squashed to death
you wish not to be...

2
00:00:03,363 --> 00:00:07,063
...sing of Svaty Vaclav and his victory."
- Who the hell is Svaty Vaclav?

3
00:00:07,234 --> 00:00:10,104
- Walls are getting closer.
- Oh, boy. Happy place, happy place.

4
00:00:10,304 --> 00:00:13,204
(Sheldon:)Svaty Vaclav was the Duke of Bohemia.

5
00:00:13,373 --> 00:00:14,933
Ten seconds from getting crushed.

6
00:00:15,108 --> 00:00:17,038
(Leonard:)- Nine. Eight.
- What are we supposed to do?

7
00:00:17,210 --> 00:00:18,940
- Seven. Six. Five.
- Wait, wait.

8
00:00:19,112 --> 00:00:21,672
(Sheldon:)Svaty Vaclav is better known
as Good King Wenceslaus...

9
00:00:21,848 --> 00:00:24,178
...from the Christmas carol.
- Never heard of it.

10
00:00:24,351 --> 00:00:27,081
(Howard:)Must be the one Christmas song
not written by a Jewish guy.

11
00:00:27,854 --> 00:00:30,554
- Three. Two.
- Somebody sing the damn song.

12
00:00:30,824 --> 00:00:34,124
(Sheldon:)Good King Wenceslas looked out
On the feast of Stephen

13
00:00:34,294 --> 00:00:38,194
When the snow lay round about
Deep and crisp and even

14
00:00:38,365 --> 00:00:39,525
(Leonard:)Walls are getting slower.

15
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:43,070
(Sheldon:)Brightly shone the moon that night
Though the frost was cruel

16
00:00:43,236 --> 00:00:48,006
(Sheldon:)When a poor man came in sight
Gath'ring winter fuel

17
00:00:52,212 --> 00:00:55,302
- The walls stop. You're safe.
- That was amazing, Sheldon.

18
00:00:55,482 --> 00:00:56,952
- How'd you know that?
- Simple.

19
00:00:57,117 --> 00:01:00,087
(Sheldon:)I combined a well-known historical fact
about Bohemia...

